---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
import AdSlot from '../../components/AdSlot.astro';
const faqs = [
  { q: "How strong is the protection?", a: "PDFSherpa uses standard 128-bit PDF encryption, which every PDF reader supports. A long password matters more than anything else: use at least 10 characters with words and numbers." },
  { q: "Can I recover the PDF if I forget the password?", a: "No. There is no backdoor and PDFSherpa never sees your password. Keep the password somewhere safe, or keep an unprotected copy on your own device." },
  { q: "How do I send the password?", a: "Use a different channel from the file. For example, email the PDF and send the password by text message or tell it on a call." },
];
---
<GuideLayout slug="password-protect-pdf" faqs={faqs}>
<p><strong>Short answer:</strong> open <a href="/protect-pdf">Protect PDF</a>, select your file, type a password twice and click <strong>Protect PDF</strong>. Anyone opening the downloaded file must enter that password first.</p>

  <h2>Step by step</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open <a href="/protect-pdf">pdfsherpa.com/protect-pdf</a> and select the PDF.</li>
    <li>Enter a password and repeat it.</li>
    <li>Click <strong>Protect PDF</strong>. The first time, the PDF engine downloads once.</li>
    <li>Download the protected file and test it: it should ask for the password when opened.</li>
  </ol>

  <AdSlot variant="inline" slot="guide-article" />

  <h2>Choosing a good password</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Use at least 10 characters. Three random words with a number, like <em>river-lamp-47-cloud</em>, are strong and easy to type.</li>
    <li>Don’t use your name, phone number, birthday or ID number, especially if the document itself contains them.</li>
    <li>Use a different password for each recipient when the documents are sensitive.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to protect a PDF</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Payslips, bank statements and tax documents sent by email.</li>
    <li>Copies of passports, ID cards and certificates.</li>
    <li>Medical reports and contracts.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Good to know</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Protection applies to the downloaded copy. Your original file on your device stays unprotected.</li>
    <li>Do other edits first. Most tools, including PDFSherpa, need the PDF unlocked before they can change it.</li>
    <li>To remove the password later, use <a href="/unlock-pdf">Unlock PDF</a> with the same password.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>Encryption happens in your browser with Ghostscript compiled to WebAssembly. Your file and password are never sent anywhere.</p>
</GuideLayout>
